{"id": "EUVD-2026-82219", "enisaUuid": "be696bca-574d-3b79-a13b-aef5d4848fdd", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nbpf: Mark tracing_multi trampolines as ftrace managed\n\nSince tracing_multi link does not set ftrace_managed, it would fail to\nrelease the tracing_multi link when attaching tracing_multi link and\nthen attaching fentry link.\n\n[    3.714215] WARNING: kernel/bpf/trampoline.c:1727 at bpf_trampoline_multi_detach+0x20b/0x240, CPU#1: test_progs/97\n...\n[    3.733170]  bpf_tracing_multi_link_release+0x14/0x30\n[    3.733890]  bpf_link_free+0x58/0x130\n[    3.734414]  bpf_link_release+0x23/0x30\n\nFix it by setting 'ftrace_managed = true' in register_fentry_multi().", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:11:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:05:44", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/280145253fd38fa975cc04963ddaf74c7f415011", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/30bdd6d1384d894931f113eb595636092d8e650c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-93111", "GHSA-285f-2chv-p9fq"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f50201b-6a1f-36b7-88c6-89a4a2a80be5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "17f1a6e2-f345-3c95-90ab-a5050bb567fa", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "4a66bf56-758c-360b-861d-9b225e70b0e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "571befb2-e0c9-3c45-bfb7-371d1c328d4d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aef4dfa790b22d8052cfb78044eadbe03c876c39 <30bdd6d1384d894931f113eb595636092d8e650c"}, {"id": "f0889e64-c2a2-3399-ae6f-d1f203e1d89e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "aef4dfa790b22d8052cfb78044eadbe03c876c